    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.snippets\n\n### Question\n\nHello,\r\n\r\nI have read the help pages in neovim and the documentation but couldn't find anything on how to setup mini.snippets/mini.completion with friendly-snippets. I dont have a snippets folder or custom snippets just want the friendly-snippets. How could I set it up. I have mason-lspconfig but if there is simpler/easier ways to explain it, please do leave them. Any help would be greatly appreciated and I can provide any information needed.",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.snippets</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Hello,</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have read the help pages in neovim and the documentation but couldn't find anything on how to setup mini.snippets/mini.completion with friendly-snippets. I dont have a snippets folder or custom snippets just want the friendly-snippets. How could I set it up. I have mason-lspconfig but if there is simpler/easier ways to explain it, please do leave them. Any help would be greatly appreciated and I can provide any information needed.</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.snippets\nQuestion\nHello,\nI have read the help pages in neovim and the documentation but couldn't find anything on how to setup mini.snippets/mini.completion with friendly-snippets. I dont have a snippets folder or custom snippets just want the friendly-snippets. How could I set it up. I have mason-lspconfig but if there is simpler/easier ways to explain it, please do leave them. Any help would be greatly appreciated and I can provide any information needed.",
